    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our lineup construction prioritizes high-ceiling matchups against soft pitching rotations, headlined by **James Wood** (76.27) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.97). **James Wood** earns the top spot in our rankings due to an elite .437 xwOBA and an aggressive leadoff position against J.T. Ginn, while **Mickey Moniak** benefits from a massive 14% boost from a favorable park environment and a soft matchup against Lowder. Similarly, **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.92) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (72.71) remain \u201cStrong\u201d starts, capitalizing on juicy SP_xERA figures north of 4.50, which provides us the necessary offensive buffer to mitigate some of the volatility inherent in our middle-infield selections.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Austin Riley**, whose score of 52.16 narrowly missed the cut. While **Austin Riley** offers pedigree, the optimizer favored the platoon-advantaged daily efficiency of **Isaac Paredes** (56.12) and the order-based upside of **Gabriel Moreno** (57.09). We are also keeping a watchful eye on our \"Lineup Pending\" players; while **Zach McKinstry** (49.61) is currently slated for a start, his low floor against a tough arm in Grayson Rodriguez makes him a candidate for a late-afternoon swap if the final batting orders shift. Furthermore, while **Corbin Carroll** (69.43) remains a core start for his speed, he faces an \"Elite Hold\" pitcher, which slightly tempers his stolen base potential compared to his usual output. Manage your game caps accordingly, as we are looking to capitalize on the 4.00+ xERA matchups across the board while hedging against the remaining unknowns in the late games.",
